    <string name="weather_about_sun_moon_rise_set">The rise time is when the sun or moon first appears above the horizon. The set time is when the sun or moon fully disappears below the horizon</string>
    <string name="weather_about_dawn_dusk">Dawn is the period of light in the sky just before sunrise. Dusk is the period of fading light in the sky just after sunset</string>
    <string name="weather_about_pressure">Mean sea level pressure, a measure of how much the atmosphere is pressing down, adjusted to sea level. Watching how it changes can provide an early indication of weather changes. Pressure falling usually means unsettled weather is approaching, while pressure rising often means conditions are becoming more stable</string>
